    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27300" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lūtum</span></b> , i, n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a plant used in
				dyeing yellow, yellow-weed. dyer's-weed, weld</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jam croceo mutabit vellera luto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 4, 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 33, 5, 26, § 87</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
			14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a yellow color,
				yellow</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. Cir. 316</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimius luto corpora tingit amor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib. 1,
					9</span></i>
			 (8), 52 Heyne ad loc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
